{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1556279-resources-for-learning-more-about-korean-mythology","id":1556279,"title":"Resources for learning more about Korean Mythology?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-12-06T20:36:44-08:00","id":1556279,"title":"Resources for learning more about Korean Mythology?","content":"I've had an idea for a Scion game involving Korean Mythology, since I wanted something a bit different compared to just Chinese and Japanese myths. Unfortunately, I haven't found much online that's easily accessible. I'm not sure if its because as a largely oral tradition thing that the caretakers of the faith don't want their stories published everywhere, or if its just a language barrier getting in the way in this case. Does anyone know of any online resources that could be used for researching this subject more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T04:55:23-08:00","id":1556284,"title":"","content":"The first resource is the University of California library catalog. It can be accessed online. It's the most likely place in the USA to find serious information on East Asian cultures. Find books on the subject and interlibrary loan them.<br /> <br /> Going to Amazon and typing in <b>Korean Mythology </b>is also worth a try.<br /> <br /> Looking online to see if the University libraries of Australia and New Zealand can be accessed is also worth a try. <br /> <br /> Going to the Government of South Korea's website and simply asking questions might work too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T05:01:00-08:00","id":1556285,"title":"","content":"Went to Amazon. Yes there are multiple books on Korean mythology. I don't know how good they are. Bonus, Korean folktales and fairy tales also show up. So at least a start. Interlibrary loan the titles that look good to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-25T13:06:19-07:00","id":1559015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1556279-resources-for-learning-more-about-korean-mythology#post1556279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had an idea for a Scion game involving Korean Mythology, since I wanted something a bit different compared to just Chinese and Japanese myths. Unfortunately, I haven't found much online that's easily accessible. I'm not sure if its because as a largely oral tradition thing that the caretakers of the faith don't want their stories published everywhere, or if its just a language barrier getting in the way in this case. Does anyone know of any online resources that could be used for researching this subject more?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you do this, I would love to know more! It is my understanding that there is no single Korean mythology, but different mythologies from the different kingdoms that came to make up Korea. I started doing a little research for a kumiho (Korean fox shifter) storyguide character in my game, who started out as a villain's henchman, but has now become a romantic interest. Kumiho have a much darker reputation in Korea than their fox-shifter counterparts in China, Japan and Vietnam, but they didn't always. The Korean kingdom of Silla once had a much more positive view of fox spirits, before political upheavals and the arrival of Confucianism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28946-pryderi","name":"Pryderi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-27T08:51:50-07:00","id":1559043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1556279-resources-for-learning-more-about-korean-mythology#post1556279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had an idea for a Scion game involving Korean Mythology, since I wanted something a bit different compared to just Chinese and Japanese myths. Unfortunately, I haven't found much online that's easily accessible. I'm not sure if its because as a largely oral tradition thing that the caretakers of the faith don't want their stories published everywhere, or if its just a language barrier getting in the way in this case. Does anyone know of any online resources that could be used for researching this subject more?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have read that Kim does not poop, and can telepathically speak to dolphins.<br /> <br /> Clearly he is the Scion of some kind of ocean deity!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-28T01:54:19-07:00","id":1559052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1556279-resources-for-learning-more-about-korean-mythology?p=1559043#post1559043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have read that Kim does not poop, and can telepathically speak to dolphins.<br /> <br /> Clearly he is the Scion of some kind of ocean deity!</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the myth making of actual North Korea (read <b>The Cleanest Race</b> a work analyzing North Korea's story about itself it tells to its own people) the idea of North Korea seeking to literally deify its leader in the Scion universe is disturbingly plausible. As we were told in the first edition's chapter on the Celestial Bureaucracy some of the Gods are communists. The idea of a committee of gods promoting a communist dictatorship to promote their ideas is scary and fits the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-28T09:39:23-07:00","id":1559063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1556279-resources-for-learning-more-about-korean-mythology?p=1559052#post1559052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given the myth making of actual North Korea (read <b>The Cleanest Race</b> a work analyzing North Korea's story about itself it tells to its own people) the idea of North Korea seeking to literally deify its leader in the Scion universe is disturbingly plausible. As we were told in the first edition's chapter on the Celestial Bureaucracy some of the Gods are communists. The idea of a committee of gods promoting a communist dictatorship to promote their ideas is scary and fits the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly certain Egypt did the same thing, by claiming their pharaohs were literally the children of Ra.<br /> <br /> During the days of imperial Japan, the people were raised from birth to believe that their emperor was a living god.<br /> <br /> There are definitely other examples throughout history, but those are the only two which immediately come to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T02:03:53-07:00","id":1559713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1556279-resources-for-learning-more-about-korean-mythology?p=1559052#post1559052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given the myth making of actual North Korea (read <b>The Cleanest Race</b> a work analyzing North Korea's story about itself it tells to its own people) the idea of North Korea seeking to literally deify its leader in the Scion universe is disturbingly plausible. As we were told in the first edition's chapter on the Celestial Bureaucracy some of the Gods are communists. The idea of a committee of gods promoting a communist dictatorship to promote their ideas is scary and fits the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, after giving it some thought, the Celestial Bureaucracy being communist might not be quite as terrible as it sounds.<br /> <br /> Hear. Me. Out.<br /> <br /> Normal bureaucracies are a mind numbing, exhausting hell hole of government oversight and red tape. But the PSP of the pantheon has made it operate with divine efficiency. You don't need to worry about paper work going missing, or not having the proper forms, or having to revisit the office 4 fucking times, because the people at the desk keep coming up with yet more information you failed to provide the last time you spoke.<br /> <br /> So, while communism in real life may be a complete and utter failure on every conceivable level, it's possible that the Celestial Bureaucracy could find a way to make it work as intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T03:45:00-07:00","id":1559714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1556279-resources-for-learning-more-about-korean-mythology?p=1559713#post1559713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually, after giving it some thought, the Celestial Bureaucracy being communist might not be quite as terrible as it sounds.<br /> <br /> Hear. Me. Out.<br /> <br /> Normal bureaucracies are a mind numbing, exhausting hell hole of government oversight and red tape. But the PSP of the pantheon has made it operate with divine efficiency. You don't need to worry about paper work going missing, or not having the proper forms, or having to revisit the office 4 fucking times, because the people at the desk keep coming up with yet more information you failed to provide the last time you spoke.<br /> <br /> So, while communism in real life may be a complete and utter failure on every conceivable level, it's possible that the Celestial Bureaucracy could find a way to make it work as intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually a Marxist in most ways. But the type of &quot;Communism&quot; followed in China and North Korea is more closely related to fascism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T06:02:48-07:00","id":1559715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1556279-resources-for-learning-more-about-korean-mythology?p=1559714#post1559714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm actually a Marxist in most ways. But the type of &quot;Communism&quot; followed in China and North Korea is more closely related to fascism.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet the one followed by the Soviets collapsed in in the early 90's.<br /> <br /> Like I said, it's a failure on every level. It has never worked in its entire history.<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> But that may be something that the pantheon doesn't have to worry about. Using their PsP, they could turn their corner of heaven into the idealized version of what communism is trying to achieve, and then use that as a basis to give their worshipers something to strive for.<br /> <br /> It's an interesting premise, at the very least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T08:15:00-07:00","id":1559724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1556279-resources-for-learning-more-about-korean-mythology?p=1559715#post1559715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet the one followed by the Soviets collapsed in in the early 90's.<br /> <br /> Like I said, it's a failure on every level. It has never worked in its entire history.<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------</div> </div> </div> </div>Lenin mainly read right-wing authors as a young man and was a great admirer of his younger contemporary Ivan Ilyin. Lenin and Stalin were both Marxist because it was fashionable. Their personal instincts were fascist. Most 20th century &quot;Marxism&quot; is Leninism, Fascism with a Marxist Face so to speak. Love him or loathe him Marx wanted to set people free. We can agree he wasn't good about his chosen path. Lenin never had any use for freedom he, Stalin, Putin, and the North Korean Communists, want control, absolute control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> But that may be something that the pantheon doesn't have to worry about. Using their PsP, they could turn their corner of heaven into the idealized version of what communism is trying to achieve, and then use that as a basis to give their worshipers something to strive for.<br /> <br /> It's an interesting premise, at the very least. </div> </div> </div>Given the total divergence between their words and their actions, you'd have to wonder what their dream society would really be like.<br /> <br /> By the way, for centuries people said &quot;Democracy always fails.&quot; Many Europeans still say it. It seems that it wasn't until we had both the Printing Press and the need to have a largely literate population that democracy became workable. Given that Capitalism and State Capitalism (which is pretty much fascism) are unsustainablly collapsing the birth rate, I think we'll figure out Socialism or go extinct. <br /> <br /> But I'm way off topic. Forgive me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 05-03-2026, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T11:35:45-07:00","id":1559727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1556279-resources-for-learning-more-about-korean-mythology?p=1559724#post1559724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But I'm way off topic. Forgive me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's alright. I just thought that it would have made an interesting experiment and decided to share my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-04T12:33:29-07:00","id":1559764,"title":"","content":"Speaking of North Korea while being more on topic, you can\u2019t really tackle the question of Korea\u2019s place within the mythic World of Scion 2e while also tackling the difficult question of North Korea\u2019s place. How are Scions, Denizens and Titanspawn treated by the North Korean government? What\u2019s the Korean Gods\u2019 opinion of the North-South divide, and how does it affect their activities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T07:50:28-07:00","id":1559922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChronoRebel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1556279-resources-for-learning-more-about-korean-mythology?p=1559764#post1559764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of North Korea while being more on topic, you can\u2019t really tackle the question of Korea\u2019s place within the mythic World of Scion 2e while also tackling the difficult question of North Korea\u2019s place. How are Scions, Denizens and Titanspawn treated by the North Korean government? What\u2019s the Korean Gods\u2019 opinion of the North-South divide, and how does it affect their activities?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two possible ways this could go.<br /> <br /> Option A) Scions and Titanspawn are kept under the absolute heaviest forms of regulation that the government can feasibly get away with, so as to not threaten the iron fisted tyranny of the nation's supreme leader.<br /> <br /> <br /> Option B) Scions and the North Korean government respect the gentleman's agreement of not fucking with each other, and stick to dealing with their own issues. Scions might get involved if a Denizen or Titanspawn decide they're going to rock the boat, but would otherwise stay out of government affairs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-16T15:48:26-07:00","id":1560033,"title":"","content":"I admit I was hoping for a collection of references that draw from the beliefs present during/predating the Three Kingdoms era.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-18T09:01:25-07:00","id":1560062,"title":"","content":"For my pantheon for Korea (the Sin-dang [work in progress] name), I mainly used the Encyclopedia of Korean Folk Literature, maintained by the National Folk Museum as reference: <a href=\"https://archive.org/search?query=creator%3A%22National+Folk+Museum+of+Korea%22\" target=\"_blank\">https://archive.org/search?query=cre...um+of+Korea%22</a><br /> <br /> The encyclopedia has been my primary source of information about the pantheon, culture, and potential NPCs and characters there but Korea is currently a minor pantheon for the campaign I'm running.<br /> <br /> The texts are available on Web Archive. <br /> <br /> The preliminary list of major deities I have are: Hwanin, Bari/Pari Gongju, Chilseongsin (the Seven Stars of the Big Dipper: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chilsongmun\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chilsongmun</a>)<br /> Titans being Seokga and Mireuk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Pantheon(s):<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LMQFZLq3NrOHs2cp7OWnfukuHCNI4h_0/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Nat, the Spirits of Myanmar</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WDvOmQCR3a25WbVowfe8KgGbGLU0yzX3/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Phi, the Spirits of the Tai People</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13670-svarogg","name":"Svarogg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13670_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-21T04:01:42-07:00","id":1560140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Svarogg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1556279-resources-for-learning-more-about-korean-mythology?p=1560062#post1560062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For my pantheon for Korea (the Sin-dang [work in progress] name), I mainly used the Encyclopedia of Korean Folk Literature, maintained by the National Folk Museum as reference: <a href=\"https://archive.org/search?query=creator%3A%22National+Folk+Museum+of+Korea%22\" target=\"_blank\">https://archive.org/search?query=cre...um+of+Korea%22</a><br /> <br /> The encyclopedia has been my primary source of information about the pantheon, culture, and potential NPCs and characters there but Korea is currently a minor pantheon for the campaign I'm running.<br /> <br /> The texts are available on Web Archive.<br /> <br /> The preliminary list of major deities I have are: Hwanin, Bari/Pari Gongju, Chilseongsin (the Seven Stars of the Big Dipper: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chilsongmun\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chilsongmun</a>)<br /> Titans being Seokga and Mireuk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sin-dang? According to Wikipedia, the Korean gods are jsut called &quot;shin&quot; or &quot;geom&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-22T16:12:41-07:00","id":1560157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChronoRebel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1556279-resources-for-learning-more-about-korean-mythology?p=1560140#post1560140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sin-dang? According to Wikipedia, the Korean gods are jsut called &quot;shin&quot; or &quot;geom&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the Wikipedia page for <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Korean_shamanism\" target=\"_blank\">Korean shamanism</a>:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Korean traditional religion, the deities are called <i>janggunsin</i>, and typically take human form. The pantheon of deities, which has changed over time, is termed <i>sindang</i>, with over 130 Musok divinities having been identified. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_